# One byte sequence for tracked text, on every platform and in every clone.
#
# Without this, what a working tree holds depends on each clone's local
# `core.autocrlf`, which no tree records and no reviewer can see. A contributor
# whose checkout carries a carriage return per line sends a one-line edit as a
# whole-file diff, and the review that mattered is buried under it. The same
# difference makes a formatter report a clean tree as failing, on a machine
# where nothing is wrong with the code.
#
# `text=auto` leaves the text-or-binary judgement to git. `eol=lf` fixes what a
# checkout produces, so the answer no longer comes from a setting each clone
# chose for itself.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Formats whose bytes are the content. Marking them binary keeps git from
# rewriting a byte inside a recorded archive response, an image or an archive.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.fits binary
*.whl binary
